  "slug": "data-transform",
  "title": "Data transform",
  "summary": "Select by JSON path, map, filter, sort, group and aggregate, pivot, de-duplicate and join lists of records, and convert CSV to JSON and back.",
  "description": "Data transform reshapes lists of records inside a workflow, the work that otherwise takes loops and a chain of collection nodes. Pick values out of an API response with a JSON path (order.lines[*].sku), rename and nest fields, filter with conditions such as status = paid and amount >= 500, sort on several keys, group by one or more fields with count, sum, average, minimum, maximum and distinct counts, pivot values into columns or unpivot columns into rows, and remove duplicates by chosen fields.\n\nJoin combines two lists on matching keys (inner, left, right or full), for example orders with the managers of their regions, and reports what did not match. CSV to JSON parses spreadsheet exports to RFC 4180 (quoted fields, embedded commas and line breaks, header row, number and boolean inference) and JSON to CSV writes lists back out with chosen columns, CRLF line endings and protection against formula injection. Everything runs in the sandbox with no network or data access.",
  "icon": "shuffle",
  "tags": [
    "data",
    "json",
    "csv",
    "group by",
    "pivot",
    "join"
  ],
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "changelog": [
